{"hw":"φιλόπολις","html":"<div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">φιλόπολις</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">φιλόπολις</span>, <span class=\"lex-gram\">ὁ</span>, <span class=\"lex-gram\">ἡ</span>, poet. <span class=\"lex-orth gk\">φιλόπτολις</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">E.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Rh.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">158</span> </span>: acc. <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">A</span> <span class=\"gk\">φιλόπολιν</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pi.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">O.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">4.18</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ap.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">24b</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Isoc.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">2.15</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">X.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Hier.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">5.3</span> </span>, etc.; pl. <span class=\"gk\">φιλοπόλεις</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Th.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">176</span> </span> (lyr.); also pl. <span class=\"gk\">-πόλιδες, -πόλιδας,</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">R.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">470d</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">503a</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">I</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">loving the city,</b> <span class=\"gk\">δαίμονες</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.</span> </span> l. c. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">II</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">loving one's city, patriotic,</b> <span class=\"gk\">δαίμων</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Ar.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Pl.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">726</span> </span> (where there is a play on the first sense), cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">900</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Th.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">2.60</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">6.92</span> </span>, Pl.ll.cc., etc.; <span class=\"gk\">φ. Ἡσυχία</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pi.</span> </span> l.c.; <span class=\"gk\">φ. ἀρετή</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">patriotism,</b> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Ar.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Lys.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">547</span> </span> (lyr.); so <span class=\"gk\">τὸ φιλόπολι</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Th.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">6.92</span> </span>.</div></div>"}